    "intro_html":  "Tetrazzini was named for an opera singer and built for leftovers, which is a combination you do not see every day. Spaghetti, chicken, and mushrooms get folded into a cream sauce, topped with mozzarella, and baked until the edges go brown and chewy. Those crispy edges are the reason people fight over the corner pieces. Each serving lands at {{cal}} calories and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
